  "summary": "I wrote src/main.ts, but I couldn't check it against the real engine API or see it render. `typecheck` reports one error, \"Cannot find module '@aura3d/engine'\". `node_modules/@aura3d` is empty in this sandbox, so no types or runtime were available. I followed the cheat sheet and recipes for every call. The code has never run, so I don't know whether the branch rotations and the swing sway behave as intended.\n\nWhat the file builds (seeded RNG, seed 20240611, so the same seed gives the same tree):\n- **Trunk and roots:** the trunk is 4 stacked cylinders with joint spheres, tapering from radius 0.98 to 0.42. A cone flares at the base, with 8 two-segment surface roots going into the mound.\n- **Branches:** 9 limbs of 2 segments each, then 2 more levels of branches. That gives about 100 tapering branches in total.\n- **Foliage:** about 57 leaf clumps, each a group of two spheres. They use 6 autumn tones: red, orange, gold, olive, green and burnt orange.\n- **Details:**\n  - A dark hollow with a bark lip and a knot on the trunk.\n  - 80 fallen leaves as instances, plus 4 mushrooms.\n  - A rope swing with two ropes and a plank seat, hanging from the first limb. It sways each frame.\n- **Scene:**\n  - A grassy mound sits on a ground plane, under a gradient sky.\n  - There's a hemisphere light and a shadow-casting key light.\n  - The orbit camera auto-rotates and frames the whole tree.\n- **Flags:** after `await app.ready()` and one more `requestAnimationFrame`, it sets `window.__EVAL_READY__ = true` and `window.__TASK_STATE__ = { ready, branchCount, foliageClumpCount, seed }`.\n\nTo orient each cylinder, I put it in a Y-rotation group wrapping an X-rotation group, so Euler order doesn't matter. This assumes a standard right-handed rotation sign.\n\n",
